            <ArticleTitle>A white flapping structure in the coronary artery lumen observed by angioscopy after coronary thrombolysis--is this the &quot;ruptured atheroma&quot; that initiated the acute myocardial infarction?</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>580-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The lumen of the coronary artery after thrombolysis using urokinase was successfully observed in patients with acute myocardial infarction. A white flapping material, resembling a ruptured atherosclerotic plaque, was seen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
